protection from the court.

254
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,082
- You had a hundred bucks here,

255
00:11:47,082 --> 00:11:48,417
how come you're
hoppin' freights?

256
00:11:48,417 --> 00:11:51,253
- It's kinda hard
to hop a plane.

257
00:11:51,253 --> 00:11:53,380
- Well, you aren't used
to travelin' this way.

258
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,548
This is something new to you.

259
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,050
You don't even know how
to handle yourself yet.

260
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,052
- I got separated from
my band trip, okay?

261
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,512
- Meaning what?

262
00:12:00,512 --> 00:12:03,432
- Meaning you don't know how
to hang on to what's yours.

263
00:12:03,432 --> 00:12:04,642
If I give this back to you,

264
00:12:04,642 --> 00:12:06,143
somebody else will just
take it away again.

265
00:12:06,143 --> 00:12:08,895
- Good idea, you'd better hang
on to my clothes then, too.

266
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:09,730
- What's your name, kid?

267
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:11,440
- Sex Poodle, oh.

268
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:12,273
- Danny.

269
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:14,818
Danny Winslow.

270
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:18,655
- Bix Dugan.
- Big Stupid?

271
00:12:18,655 --> 00:12:22,325
- Mr. Stupid, can I
have my wallet back now?

272
00:12:26,705 --> 00:12:28,415
- War-torn Wisconsin.

273
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:38,967
- Wow, you got me a wallet,
and I just lost mine!

274
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:42,555
- If you'd said you
stole it, I'da kept it.

275
00:12:44,932 --> 00:12:47,433
- How does that make you feel?

276
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:51,105
- Well, you better get
some sleep, Danny boy.

277
00:12:51,105 --> 00:12:52,815
- I can't sleep now,
I'm too excited.

278
00:12:52,815 --> 00:12:54,900
- I think maybe you
got a long way to go.

279
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,443
- And I'm gonna take you there.

280
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:02,448
- Hey, I call the
top bunk. (laughs)

281
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:07,120
- Hey, are we bound for glory
right now, Mr. Big Stupid?

282
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:13,418
- Rail, rail against the dying
of the light, rail. (laughs)

283
00:13:16,547 --> 00:13:18,215
You were incredible.

284
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:21,635
- Bix?
- Can I have a glass of water?

285
00:13:21,635 --> 00:13:22,970
- Are ya asleep?

286
00:13:24,137 --> 00:13:24,972
- Yeah.

287
00:13:27,725 --> 00:13:28,850
- I'm thinking.

288
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:29,810
- Can we snuggle?

289
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:31,562
- Don't, you'll weaken the team.

290
00:13:31,562 --> 00:13:33,438
- I wrote a poem about you
while you were sleeping.

291
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,357
- Where you going, Bix?

292
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,235
- Back to sleep.

293
00:13:41,822 --> 00:13:44,325
- I'm serious, wake
up and talk to me.

294
00:13:44,325 --> 00:13:45,158
Where ya headed?

295
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:47,160
- This is getting weird.

296
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:51,082
- Wherever this train's
headed, I ain't particular.

297
00:13:51,082 --> 00:13:53,292
- Should we call ahead
and make reservations?

298
00:13:53,292 --> 00:13:55,252
- That's what I thought.

299
00:13:57,045 --> 00:14:00,090
I've got an idea.
- Toaster pastries!

300
00:14:00,090 --> 00:14:01,550
- Congratulations.

301
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:03,260
- Uh, Bix, don't laugh
at my footie pajamas

302
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:05,262
when I put 'em on, okay?

303
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,642
- All right.
- Hop on.

304
00:14:09,642 --> 00:14:11,143
- What do you want
to talk about?

305
00:14:11,143 --> 00:14:13,978
- Well, I was thinking about
changing the part in my hair.

306
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:17,733
- I was just thinking, since
you don't care where you go

307
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:20,485
just so long as you keep moving,

308
00:14:20,485 --> 00:14:22,362
why can't we travel together?

309
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,823
- I've killed a bunch of
drifters, and you could be next.

310
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:27,450
- Well, for one thing, you
got a hundred bucks, kid.

311
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,910
And I don't know whether
you know it or not,

312
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:31,538
but a conventional vagrant
don't make much money.

313
00:14:31,538 --> 00:14:33,040
- Well, the money will
be my part of the deal.

314
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,667
- You'll bring a sense of style.

315
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:38,545
- I, I'd just like to
have someone to go with.

316
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,797
- And I'll give you $10
every time you don't hit me.

317
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:42,382
- It's your loot, man.

318
00:14:42,382 --> 00:14:45,010
I guess we're stuck
with each other.

319
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:47,847
- Dear diary, I think I'm
finally becoming a real vagrant.

320
00:14:47,847 --> 00:14:49,307
Big Stupid says
he's gonna teach me

321
00:14:49,307 --> 00:14:52,392
the ins and outs of drifting.

322
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:54,312
- At my age, I
gotta be a mother.

323
00:14:54,312 --> 00:14:58,773
- Hey, this boxcar's enormous,
would you move, Danny?

324
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:03,737
- Uh, camera three
get off the track.

325
00:15:03,737 --> 00:15:05,280
Camera three, oh dear god!
(screaming)

326
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:07,617
(fun music)

327
00:15:15,165 --> 00:15:18,918
- I woke up and you
were there, I hate that.

328
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:20,503
- What's the matter?

329
00:15:20,503 --> 00:15:22,715
- Seven minutes late, raccoon
on the tracks at Brixton.

330
00:15:22,715 --> 00:15:24,800
- Could be nothin', they're
probably stoppin' for water.

331
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,343
- Is that bad, when
they stop for water?

332
00:15:26,343 --> 00:15:27,887
Do you want me to get
you some water, Bix?

333
00:15:27,887 --> 00:15:29,053
Is water a good--
- Just shut up, Danny.

334
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:29,888
- Oh.

335
00:15:33,558 --> 00:15:34,393
- Hold me.

336
00:15:36,020 --> 00:15:39,732
- Oh, it's just as I
dreamed it would be.

337
00:15:39,732 --> 00:15:42,777
- Looks like we're
about a mile from town.

338
00:15:42,777 --> 00:15:43,818
Better get off here.

339
00:15:43,818 --> 00:15:45,570
- (laughs) Never mind.

340
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:47,405
- Why don't we just take
the train all the way in?

341
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,198
- Sure, all the way
in and right to jail.

342
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:52,368
Or did you buy a ticket
for this joyride?

343
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,287
She's slowin' down, come on.

344
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:56,582
- Mr. Big Stupid, catch me.

345
00:15:57,917 --> 00:15:58,917
- Is this right?

346
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:01,087
Am I walkin' with ya right?

347
00:16:01,087 --> 00:16:05,757
- I'll always remember you,
boxcar number 1837562093.

348
00:16:05,757 --> 00:16:07,133
Bye-bye.

349
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:10,137
- I'd really like
to freshen up now.

350
00:16:12,682 --> 00:16:17,185
- Gee, I thought Vegas
would be bigger and shinier.

351
00:16:17,185 --> 00:16:19,855
- Get off the road, ya drifters!

352
00:16:22,232 --> 00:16:23,650
- Like father, like bum?

353
00:16:23,650 --> 00:16:25,818
Think about it, won't you?

354
00:16:27,237 --> 00:16:29,698
- Is that a girl, my
lord, in a flatbed Ford,

355
00:16:29,698 --> 00:16:33,077
slowin' down to take
a look at, oh, no.

356
00:16:33,077 --> 00:16:36,913
- Hey, I want you to take
this kid for me, will ya?

357
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:41,502
- Hey, can we stop for
biscuits and gravy, Big?

358
00:16:41,502 --> 00:16:43,420
- I think I sat on your keys.

359
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,047
- What town we comin' to?
- Funkytown.

360
00:16:45,047 --> 00:16:47,590
- Sherman, nice little town.

361
00:16:47,590 --> 00:16:48,550
- I'll say!

362
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:50,552
No ifs, ands, or buts.

363
00:16:50,552 --> 00:16:52,220
- Two Moon Junction.

364
00:16:53,555 --> 00:16:55,223
- Laura Petrie, no!

365
00:16:55,223 --> 00:16:56,767
- Laura Petrie, yes.

366
00:16:56,767 --> 00:17:00,645
- Actually, guys,
it's Millie Helper.

367
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:03,232
- That's real nice, ma'am,
but you're still under arrest.

368
00:17:03,232 --> 00:17:07,277
- See ya later, Carrie.
- You're so very.

369
00:17:07,277 --> 00:17:08,695
- Hey, train'll be in soon.

370
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:10,113
- Oh, it's just another freight.

371
00:17:10,113 --> 00:17:11,490
- It'll still be in soon.

372
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:12,783
- Oh, Peggy, not another one.

373
00:17:12,783 --> 00:17:14,493
- Just a half one.
- You'll get fat.

374
00:17:14,493 --> 00:17:16,703
- Johnny isn't complaining.

375
00:17:16,703 --> 00:17:18,455
- Johnny's pretty wild.

376
00:17:18,455 --> 00:17:20,082
You've been seeing
a lot of him lately.

377
00:17:20,082 --> 00:17:21,583
- Well, he's better
than nothing.

378
00:17:21,583 --> 00:17:23,043
- You haven't tried nothing.

379
00:17:23,043 --> 00:17:25,503
- You haven't been seeing
anybody, you never do.

380
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:27,547
- Oh, I can't talk to
boys the way you do.

381
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:29,758
- That's silly, Carrie.

382
00:17:29,758 --> 00:17:31,802
Besides, who has to talk?

383
00:17:31,802 --> 00:17:34,137
- Oh, I get it. (laughs)

384
00:17:34,137 --> 00:17:35,930
- Uh-oh, look who
just walked in,

385
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:38,767
Sherman's answer to
the brainless wonder.

386
00:17:38,767 --> 00:17:40,518
- Hey, it's Abe Lincoln.

387
00:17:40,518 --> 00:17:43,230
- My pa left a list of
things for you to get, Jesse.

388
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:45,315
- Some lice shampoo and a comb?

389
00:17:45,315 --> 00:17:47,650
- You understand what
you're to do now?

390
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:49,152
- I don't think you're
gettin' through, honey.

391
00:17:49,152 --> 00:17:51,280
Try drawin' pictures.
- Hey, what did I say?

392
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,823
- Jesse, I'm talking to you.

393
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:56,285
- I know, I just
like to look at ya.

394
00:17:56,285 --> 00:17:59,412
- Oh wow, maybe I should
leave you two lovebirds alone.

395
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,247
- No.

396
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,748
- Supposed to go
down to the store

397
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,627
and get your pa some
supplies, is that right?

398
00:18:04,627 --> 00:18:06,628
- Yes, that's right.
- As a young man,

399
00:18:06,628 --> 00:18:09,047
Garrison Keillor was
shunned by his friends.

400
00:18:09,047 --> 00:18:13,010
- Thank you, Jesse.
(growling)

401
00:18:13,010 --> 00:18:15,762
- I wish that I
was Jesse's girl.

402
00:18:18,682 --> 00:18:20,350
- Smells like Derby
canned tamales.

403
00:18:20,350 --> 00:18:23,520
- Honey, you're trembling.
- Am I?

404
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,147
I don't ever want to
be alone with him,

405
00:18:25,147 --> 00:18:26,398
just the thought of it--

406
00:18:26,398 --> 00:18:28,650
- Oh, stop it, Carrie,
for goodness sakes.

407
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:30,943
He's as harmless as a pup.
- Yeah, Cujo.

408
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:33,072
- Everybody knows it.

409
00:18:33,072 --> 00:18:35,448
The poor idiot likes
you, that's all.

410
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:37,533
- It's the way you're dressed,
who wouldn't leer at you?

411
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:40,870
- What you need is a
man, honey, I know.

412
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:44,625
You'll see, one'll come
along, they always do.

413
00:18:44,625 --> 00:18:47,418
- (laughs) That's our Midge!

414
00:18:47,418 --> 00:18:50,880
♪ Green eyed lady, sexy lady ♪

415
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:55,218
- I've had enough of you
two, now get out, out, out!

416
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:59,347
- Big, should I have not put
my head in the driver's lap?

417
00:18:59,347 --> 00:19:00,557
Was that wrong?

418
00:19:01,683 --> 00:19:03,935
- Look out, Sherman,
here we come!

419
00:19:03,935 --> 00:19:05,770
- Shut up, Danny.
- Oh.

420
00:19:08,607 --> 00:19:10,608
- Ever been here before?

421
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:12,235
- Small towns are all the same,

422
00:19:12,235 --> 00:19:14,195
you seen one, you seen 'em all.

423
00:19:14,195 --> 00:19:15,447
- Well, the zoning's different.

424
00:19:15,447 --> 00:19:16,865
- I'm hungry, let's
get something to eat.

425
00:19:16,865 --> 00:19:18,325
- That's a good idea.

426
00:19:18,325 --> 00:19:22,787
- You're catchin' on, kid, that
was very insightful of you.

427
00:19:22,787 --> 00:19:24,288
- We're hungry, but
I thought of it.

428
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:25,748
You know, you think that
could be my new job, Bix?

429
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:28,085
Decidin' when to eat?
- Shut up, Danny.

430
00:19:28,085 --> 00:19:29,628
- You won't tell your old
man I was late, will ya?

431
00:19:29,628 --> 00:19:31,505
- No, of course not, but--
- But what?

432
00:19:31,505 --> 00:19:33,090
- You shouldn't have brought
her in here with you.

433
00:19:33,090 --> 00:19:34,340
- Oh, what's the harm?

434
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,967
- You know how Pa
feels about her,

435
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:38,678
he's told you time and again
not to let Sadie in here.

436
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:40,847
- How is he gonna know,
unless you tell him?

437
00:19:40,847 --> 00:19:41,848
Let me worry about it.

438
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:43,350
- Hey Mel, kiss my grits!

439
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,352
- Tom, don't ever
say that again.

440
00:19:45,352 --> 00:19:47,645
- Sorry.
- Okay, what'll it be?

441
00:19:47,645 --> 00:19:50,190
- Well first, a little respect,
we ain't bummin' a meal.

442
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:52,067
- [Pete] Oh, money men, huh?

443
00:19:52,067 --> 00:19:53,860
Well now ain't that interestin'.

444
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:56,238
You're gonna have to excuse
the looks of this place,

445
00:19:56,238 --> 00:19:58,407
we ain't used to caterin'
to the carriage trade.

446
00:19:58,407 --> 00:19:59,617
- Ouch.

447
00:19:59,617 --> 00:20:00,867
- Well do you think
you could get back here

448
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,618
with a menu before
the food goes bad?

449
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:03,828
- Food's bad already.

450
00:20:03,828 --> 00:20:06,080
- The girl will
wait on you, bud.

451
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,415
- What is this, the Sad Cafe?

452
00:20:07,415 --> 00:20:09,042
- Go on up there and
wait on those clowns.

453
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:12,712
- All right.
(circus music)

454
00:20:12,712 --> 00:20:14,213
- Hi, I'm Midge,
can I start you out

455
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:17,092
with some grilled mahi-mahi
in a grapefruit cream sauce?

456
00:20:17,092 --> 00:20:18,093
- Don't fall in
love with us, baby,

457
00:20:18,093 --> 00:20:20,262
we'll hurt you every time.

458
00:20:22,347 --> 00:20:24,515
- Well, have you made
up your minds yet?

459
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:26,518
- Have I ever.
(mimicking alarms)

460
00:20:26,518 --> 00:20:29,145
- Dive, dive!
- Oh, you mean the order?

461
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:31,857
Well I'll have scrambled
eggs and coffee.

462
00:20:31,857 --> 00:20:33,108
- Okay, you want juice, salad,

463
00:20:33,108 --> 00:20:35,777
roll, grapefruit
half, or pudding?

464
00:20:36,695 --> 00:20:38,738
- Rosie, the early years.

465
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:40,365
- I didn't think life
could get any worse.

466
00:20:40,365 --> 00:20:43,493
I'm gonna go turn on the gas.

467
00:20:43,493 --> 00:20:44,995
- I've got a feeling
you're spending

468
00:20:44,995 --> 00:20:46,830
the rest of our
money right here.

469
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:48,248
- You're not ready
for quits yet, Danny.

470
00:20:48,248 --> 00:20:49,750
- Well now, what I got
in mind, Danny boy,

471
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:51,208
shouldn't cost me.

472
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:55,213
- We're drifters, you?

473
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,133
(door opening)

474
00:20:58,133 --> 00:20:59,508
- Oh, you have
your food already.

475
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:00,968
How'd you do that?

476
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,932
- Should I use a fork, Bix?

477
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:11,813
- Say, you're new in
town, ain't ya, honey?

478
00:21:11,813 --> 00:21:13,065
- Yeah.

479
00:21:13,065 --> 00:21:15,483
- The open road is
our home, ma'am.

480
00:21:15,483 --> 00:21:19,445
- Well, come on over,
Sadie wants to talk to you.

481
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:21,907
- Suddenly this is Rain.
- Sit down, baby.

482
00:21:21,907 --> 00:21:23,283
- I like the welcome wagon here.

483
00:21:23,283 --> 00:21:25,118
- Now, tell me all
about yourself.

484
00:21:25,118 --> 00:21:30,123
- Well, I don't have any bones,
I'm just cartilage, and...

485
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,668
- Well, can I tempt
you with some desert?

486
00:21:35,045 --> 00:21:38,840
- Sorry about that earlier
sexism thing there.

487
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,883
- Is she wipin' his lap?
- No.

488
00:21:40,883 --> 00:21:42,968
- Hey, you missed a spot.

489
00:21:44,972 --> 00:21:46,932
What's your name, honey?

490
00:21:46,932 --> 00:21:48,350
- Carrie.
- I'm so very.

491
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:49,935
- [Carrie] Carrie Anders.

492
00:21:49,935 --> 00:21:52,103
- Bet you have a
lot of boyfriends,
pretty girl like you.

493
00:21:52,103 --> 00:21:55,732
- No, I'm saving myself
for the right oily drifter.

494
00:21:55,732 --> 00:21:58,902
- Condiment man,
get your condiments.

495
00:21:58,902 --> 00:22:01,488
- Jesse, put that--
- We hit a wrinkle in time!

496
